<h1 align="center">Find and use an Enchanting Altar!</h1><br/>
<p>Enchanting Altars can almost always be found in your Capital City outside of the Auction House. Ask nearby players to summon a |cffe6cc80|Hitem:1903513|h[Mystic Enchanting Altar]|h|r if one isn't up!<br/><br/>
Permanent Enchanting Altars can be found in the world. Open your World Map and look for the purple Altar icon to discover their locations. </p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\3_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Obtain an Untarnished Mystic Scroll.</h1><br/>
<p>Interact with an Enchanting Altar: <br/>
•Select the Scrolls Tab<br/>
•Select Obtain Untarnished Mystic Scroll<br/>
•Click Obtain. This costs 10 silver.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\3_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reforge your Untarnished Mystic Scroll.</h1><br/>
<p>Reforging rerolls the Mystic Enchant contained on your Mystic Scroll.<br/><br/>
You can reforge the same scroll until you find a Mystic Enhant you like. Each reforge costs a Mystic Rune. If you run out of Mystic Runes it will consume gold!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Mystic_Extracts_and_Reforging_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Keep Reforging until you earn a Mystic Extract!</h1><br/>
<p>You gain experience towards your Mystic Enchanting level each time you reforge. Gaining a new Mystic Enchanting level grants you a Mystic Extract.<br/><br/>
Make sure to keep Mystic Enchants you like. You can always obtain a new Untarnished Scroll to keep reforging.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\4_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Save a Mystic Enchant to your Enchant Collection</h1><br/>
<p>Extract a Mystic Enchant from a Mystic Scroll to permanently add it to your Enchant Collection. This collection is realm wide!<br/><br/>
Saving enchants to your collection requires a Mystic Extract.<br/><br/>
Use an Enchanting Altar, click the Scrolls Tab, the click Save to Collection on the Mystic Enchant you want to permanently save.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Mystic_Enchant_Collection_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Collect Mystic Enchants that empower your spells!</h1><br/>
<p>There is no limit to how many Extracts you can earn or Mystic Enchants you can collect!<br/><br/>
You can find Mystic Enchants that empower your current spells and archetype by reforging Mystic Scrolls or buying them from the Auction House.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Change Your Look with Transmog!</h1><br/>
<p>Transmogrification (commonly known as “mogging”) is a cosmetic system using the equipment saved in the player’s Wardrobe to overwrite the visuals of your equipped gear.<br/><br/>
When transmogging, only the appearance of your equipment changes, not the stats. This way you get the freedom to change your look without losing any of your power!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Classless Heroes Can Transmog All Types of Gear!</h1><br/>
<p>On a classless server, you have the freedom to assign any gear to its associating slot, regardless of its armor or weapon type, so you can fulfill your hero’s fantasy and look exactly the way you want to!<br/><br/>
To preview your saved cosmetics, open the Wardrobe tab in Character Advancement. In this menu, you can find various ways to customize your character, going so far as to even change shapeshift forms with Incarnations, or the very spells you cast to create your unique hero!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Preview Your Collection in the Wardrobe</h1><br/>
<p>To transmog, go to the “Items” tab in the upper menu. Use filters or the search bar to find a specific piece of gear you love, or browse each armor slot individually by clicking its icon.<br/><br/>
In this menu, you can preview all of the currently available gear in the game, but it's up to you to collect them and learn their appearance for yourself!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Let’s Mog!</h1><br/>
<p>Click on a piece of gear to select it for transmog and the preview of your character in the left menu will update with your selection.<br/><br/>
To save your transmog, click the Apply button at the top. Transmogging is never permanent, so if you change your mind later you can always Right Click an item to revert it back to its original appearance.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_5:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Transmog is Saved to the Gear Slot, Not the Equipment Itself!</h1><br/>
<p>To make Transmog as convenient as possible, your new cosmetic is saved to your equipment slot, not the piece of gear itself!<br/><br/>
This allows you the freedom to change your gear without losing your preferred appearance!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\6_6:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Look Awesome, Play Awesome!</h1><br/>
<p>You can perfect your hero’s looks at any time, and from anywhere, with the Wardrobe menu!<br/><br/>
The Wardrobe is your hub for ultimate customization of your character. Mix and match with various equipment, change your shapeshift form, or even find matching armor sets with the upper tabs. There is no limit to what you can do!<br/><br/>
And the best part… it’s all free! There is no cost to change your appearance, you can customize your character as many times as you like without restriction!</p>
